      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1904-09-24_WidnesExaminer_art0083" n="art0083">
        <head>EVENTS OF THE WEEK.</head>
        <p>EVENTS OF THE WEEK.</p>
        <p>THE THRONE OF iTALY.</p>
        <p>Following the example of the Tsarina, Queen Elena of Italy has given birth to a 'son and heir to the Italian Throne, and thus within a few weeks the succession in the case of two of the leading countries of Europe is assured in the direct line. The happy event took place last Thursday night at I i p.m. at the Royal Palace at Racconigi, and the news reached home about one o'clock on Friday morning, when celebrations immediately began, which lasted for several clays, the whole populace being wild with joy. All over Europe the announcement was re- ceived with delight, and nowhere more so than in our own country, which has of late through the good offices of King Edward become so closely allied to Italy. Congratu- lations poured in from all over Europe, and there is no happier man living to-day than King Victor. To mark his gratification he ordered a remission of sentences in the case of political and many • other prisoners, and contributed out of his privy purse the sum of a million lire ( Ltto,000) to the workmen's old age pension fund. The new baby has been</p>
      </div>
